.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-CHECK-QUALITY 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-check-quality
.Nd verify local quality records and retained review inputs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3 scripts/check-quality-process.py
.Nm python3 scripts/check-quality-process.py
.Fl Fl help
.Nm python3 scripts/check-quality-process.py
.Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This is a source-checkout developer command.
The manual title does not name an installed executable.
Run with Python 3.10 or newer from the repository root.
The checker finds its inputs relative to the script, not the working
directory.
It validates the quality inventory schema, retained review manifest identity,
listed source digests, unique IDs, coverage/gap dispositions and local file
references.
References must be existing files inside the applicable repository or snapshot
root.
It does not execute the referenced tests or authenticate reviewer sign-off.
Open gaps are expected records and do not themselves cause failure.
.Pp
The checker reads local files and emits a result; it creates no report
directory
and does not rewrite inventories or retained evidence.
Use the aggregate command for retained logs and its 60-second gate watchdog.
The standalone checker does not implement a separate elapsed-time or output
cap.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl help
Print usage and exit without performing the check.
.It Fl Fl version
Print the command version and exit.
This is not a published sys-init release identifier.
.El
.Pp
There are no ordinary operands, repair modes or output-directory options.
.Sh OUTPUT
Success prints JSON with schema sys-init-quality-check-v1, result pass,
scope, surface count and open-gap count on standard output.
Caught record or file errors print an escaped diagnostic prefixed by
quality process: on standard error, without a failure JSON object.
.Pp
For a missing reference, review its intended destination and update live
records.
For a retained-manifest mismatch, preserve the failed attempt and investigate
identity; do not regenerate historical digests to make changed evidence pass.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
There are no command-specific environment configuration variables.
Python uses its ordinary host environment; all reviewed inputs are local.
No sibling checkout, network service or downloaded tool is consulted.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa docs/quality-inventory.json
Coverage, gaps, process references and retained snapshot identity.
.It Pa docs/evidence/standards-update-2026-09-05/SHA256SUMS.json
Currently selected retained review manifest; the inventory selects the
snapshot.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Record structure and reviewed bytes passed; also help and version.
.It 1
A caught record, reference, type or filesystem error.
.It 64
Invalid arguments, with usage and diagnostics on standard error.
.El
.Pp
Unexpected interpreter failures or abrupt termination can produce a nonzero
exit without a normal result.
An absent result is not success.
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the sys-init repository root with prerequisites already provisioned:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-quality-process.py --help
python3 scripts/check-quality-process.py
.Ed
.Pp
The first invocation prints usage and exits zero.
The second prints the success JSON and exits zero only if its scoped checks
pass.
To exercise argument rejection without changing inputs:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-quality-process.py --unknown
.Ed
.Pp
This prints diagnostics on standard error and exits 64.
No root privileges are required by these examples.
Use python3 scripts/check-all.py to retain the normal check and its logs.
.Sh SEE ALSO
Repository references: docs/QUALITY-PROCESS.md and
docs/quality-inventory.json,
docs/DEVELOPMENT-CHECKS.md and docs/DOCUMENTATION-INVENTORY.md.
Render this source with the host mandoc tool for offline terminal reading.
.Sh CAVEATS
Independent technical and reader review, installed-target lookup and release
approval remain separate.
This check does not establish runtime conformance.
.Pp
Decision 0116 requires exact inventory/surface fields and documented optional
gap references, with strict types and bounded JSON before reference traversal.
Each JSON record is at most 1 MiB and 32 levels deep.
Snapshot payload reads are also limited to 1 MiB per file.
Inputs and references must be ordinary files without symlink components
at or below the checkout root.
General reference contents are not read or size-limited.
Nonblocking opens and descriptor identity checks reject selected replacements;
size and modification time are checked after reading.
These checks provide neither atomic directory traversal nor an I/O deadline.
Collections contain 1 to 1,000 entries; strings have at most 4,096 characters.
Duplicate keys, non-finite constants and malformed paths/digests reject.
One captured manifest supplies both digest verification and parsed content.
Failures retain stderr-only diagnostics and exit 1.
See docs/QUALITY-RECORDS.md for remaining filesystem and snapshot limits.
.Pp
Decision 0117 requires the complete snapshot file set to match the manifest,
excluding the manifest file itself from listed payloads.
Symlink and special snapshot entries reject; traversal allows at most 2,000
files and directories.
Final membership, listed digests and inventory/manifest bytes are rechecked.
General references and hostile concurrent filesystem changes remain separately
scoped; these checks do not provide an atomic snapshot.
